{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue","id":1511213,"title":"Kikirpg Statement issues about the W5 Preview Issue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T05:17:16-07:00","id":1511213,"title":"Kikirpg Statement issues about the W5 Preview Issue","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.kiwirpg.com/media-release/statement-on-world-of-darknesss-appropriation-of-the-likeness-of-tame-iti/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.kiwirpg.com/media-release/statement-on-world-of-darknesss-appropriation-of-the-likeness-of-tame-iti/\" target=\"_blank\"> Statement on World of Darkness&rsquo;s appropriation of the likeness of T\u0101me Iti, Kiwi RPG | K\u0113mu Whakatau O Aotearoa </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.kiwirpg.com/media-release/statement-on-world-of-darknesss-appropriation-of-the-likeness-of-tame-iti/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.kiwirpg.com/media-release/statement-on-world-of-darknesss-appropriation-of-the-likeness-of-tame-iti/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Statement from KiwiRPG chair Liam Stevens Kia ora t\u0101tou I wanted to take a moment to respond to this last week's controversy surrounding World of... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:43:30-07:00","id":1511283,"title":"","content":"It's better just don't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:25:42-07:00","id":1511314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511283#post1511283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's better just don't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really a productive response to the practices in question. Definitely don't just trace random pictures on the internet to use as the basis for professional work, for one, and if you're a producer, don't just casually throw everything into layout without asking questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:26:42-07:00","id":1511315,"title":"","content":"It's even better to work with indigenous and other minority cultures to make sure they can represent themselves in your setting KiwiRPG specifically has resources for companies like Paradox to find creatives that could make respectful Maori characters for WoD books. There are plenty of organizations for other people out there, or at least vocal activists to reach out to (even if not all specifically RPG folks, but the Wraith book on the impact of the Holocaust consulted a highly respected non-gaming, non-fiction expert, and it's considered a gold standard book for handling such sensitive topics).<br /> <br /> People want to see themselves in their games. But they want to see themselves, not a caricature of themselves, and the best way for companies to do that is to hire people from those communities to elevate their voices and make their games more appealing for being authentic and engaging.<br /> <br /> As Liam pointed out elsewhere, the video game Civilization VI wanted to have a Maori playable civilization, and the game uses real historical (or at least semi-historical as some entries in the series will go a bit more into people on the edge of history and mythology) as the leader of that civilization. So they hired people from that culture and listen to them (including hired a traditional tattoo artist to design a unique set of tattoos just for the game's representation of said leader), and the game is better for having a really fun new playable group that people from that culture feel represents their culture and history well.<br /> <br /> It might be hard for a small TTRPG company running on shoestrings to do a lot here, but Paradox is not that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:53:00-07:00","id":1511316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511314#post1511314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really a productive response to the practices in question. Definitely don't just trace random pictures on the internet to use as the basis for professional work, for one, and if you're a producer, don't just casually throw everything into layout without asking questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, in my opinion this ends up limiting the options not to mention the time that must be spent with each correction, and between us that for the WTA this cost 4 tribes, maybe more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T18:05:05-07:00","id":1511317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511315#post1511315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's even better to work with indigenous and other minority cultures to make sure they can represent themselves in your setting KiwiRPG specifically has resources for companies like Paradox to find creatives that could make respectful Maori characters for WoD books. There are plenty of organizations for other people out there, or at least vocal activists to reach out to (even if not all specifically RPG folks, but the Wraith book on the impact of the Holocaust consulted a highly respected non-gaming, non-fiction expert, and it's considered a gold standard book for handling such sensitive topics).<br /> <br /> People want to see themselves in their games. But they want to see themselves, not a caricature of themselves, and the best way for companies to do that is to hire people from those communities to elevate their voices and make their games more appealing for being authentic and engaging.<br /> <br /> As Liam pointed out elsewhere, the video game Civilization VI wanted to have a Maori playable civilization, and the game uses real historical (or at least semi-historical as some entries in the series will go a bit more into people on the edge of history and mythology) as the leader of that civilization. So they hired people from that culture and listen to them (including hired a traditional tattoo artist to design a unique set of tattoos just for the game's representation of said leader), and the game is better for having a really fun new playable group that people from that culture feel represents their culture and history well.<br /> <br /> It might be hard for a small TTRPG company running on shoestrings to do a lot here, but Paradox is not that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good thought, the problem is whether the group or representative in question does not find it insulting that their people are represented in the material in question, whether the representation is faithful or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T18:16:01-07:00","id":1511318,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you're trying to say with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T11:32:53-07:00","id":1511392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511316#post1511316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, in my opinion this ends up limiting the options not to mention the time that must be spent with each correction, and between us that for the WTA this cost 4 tribes, maybe more.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, for a lot of people, the fact that they had consultants but put them in a corner, didn't listen to them and seemed to not want to have them at all has cost them a bit more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T01:47:35-07:00","id":1511434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511392#post1511392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, for a lot of people, the fact that they had consultants but put them in a corner, didn't listen to them and seemed to not want to have them at all has cost them a bit more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the bad publicity money can buy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T06:21:30-07:00","id":1511607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511392#post1511392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, for a lot of people, the fact that they had consultants but put them in a corner, didn't listen to them and seemed to not want to have them at all has cost them a bit more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, frankly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T07:03:00-07:00","id":1511609,"title":"","content":"I admit I got no publishing experience, so grain of salt, but how hard is it to ask a person whose job it is to know these things if something is offensive? In this case it was the artist derping about, but in general it shouldn't be hard to get input.<br /> <br /> Unless they don't want to change stuff at all and are just hoping to avoid the big controversies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T08:47:54-07:00","id":1511616,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know if you lot have read hunter lines drawn in blood, but it\u2019s very clear the authors have their hands tied with their content. It\u2019s so full of trigger warnings as to be off putting obnoxious. <br /> <br /> they are trying to appease the crowd of people who are actively looking to be offended, and when you\u2019re trying to be as pan cultural and global as possible things fall through the cracks. If you don\u2019t know what\u2019s significant to a culture and you see it as \u201cthis is a defining trait of these people,\u201d chances are they\u2019re gonna do it. <br /> <br /> people are quick to jump their ass about malice, intentional racism and all of this with zero idea of who these people are behind the screen. Demonizing with zero evidence of that. This isn\u2019t to say art theft is ok, stealing someone\u2019s image certainly isn\u2019t. But if the man\u2019s pic was part of a public domain reference this can happen. <br /> <br /> stop attributing malice when it\u2019s more likely ignorance. They are TRYING. They fixed it. <br /> <br /> With the amount of cultures in the world, the variance, this is ALOT to consider. Hiring one or 2 cultural folk from one or two indigenous cultures does not cover the entire span of the world. You lot are asking for alot. Wasn\u2019t there 200 tribes alone in the pacific north west? There\u2019s 250 or so different version of Christianity. This is a large spread. They cannot possibly afford to hire enough consultants to cover all of this. <br /> <br /> and if the answer after that is \u201cthen they better not try at all,\u201d consider what that means as well. May as well go back to a euro centric game line to be safe.<br /> <br /> patience and understanding goes a long way. <br /> And this coming from my negative ass. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T10:05:32-07:00","id":1511621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511616#post1511616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know if you lot have read hunter lines drawn in blood, but it\u2019s very clear the authors have their hands tied with their content. It\u2019s so full of trigger warnings as to be off putting obnoxious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trigger warnings are there to make sure no one is legit hurt. It is the same thing as the <i>Warning: Contains nuts</i> warnings on packages.<br /> <br /> And before anyone mentions the genre; If someone is allergic to shrimp, that allergy remains regardless of the type of food made. It is the same with trigger warnings, someone might LOVE Black Dog stuff, but they cannot deal with kidnapping scenarios at all.<br /> <br /> As for assuming malice, if you are making a high-profile product you have also to accept responsibility if things go wrong. This time it was a lazy artist, but that then means you might need to rethink hiring them again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T10:12:06-07:00","id":1511623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511616#post1511616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> stop attributing malice when it\u2019s more likely ignorance. They are TRYING. They fixed it.<br /> <br /> patience and understanding goes a long way.<br /> And this coming from my negative ass.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's two sides to the coin here. Yes it may be ignorance rather than malice but after enough mistakes because of ignorance that is effectively the same as malice. You can only plead ignorance if you actively try to learn. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T10:42:45-07:00","id":1511628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511616#post1511616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know if you lot have read hunter lines drawn in blood, but it\u2019s very clear the authors have their hands tied with their content. It\u2019s so full of trigger warnings as to be off putting obnoxious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now have read it and it feels more like a case of bad aesthetic choices. Both layout-wise by putting those things at the beginning of each chapter (and needlessly repeating it with the NPC-write-ups) and giving it a little &quot;box&quot; so-to speak is weird and calling it &quot;Content Warnings&quot; is also weird. After all, what it actually is trying to do is give Storyteller-advice with the notion of &quot;If you want to tone down the darkness of this story, here are the dials where you can turn things down a notch.&quot; Like, here's an example from Chapter 1 for people who don't have the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CONTENT WARNINGS<br /> The ghosts in this story are from the 1930s. Some of them are horrible people; others have major problems. One is casually sexist, one is extremely racist, and one is a morphine addict. Discuss this content with your group up front. If they\u2019re uncomfortable or reluctant, cut it or rework it to suit. Ignore Mrs. Iris Henderson\u2019s gender role expectations, remove Sergeant Lawrence entirely, and make Tollence destitute but not addicted. Do not hesitate, do not second guess yourself: this is a game, and nobody should ever be hurt by playing.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Like I said, if you had it just put it at the beginning of the chapter after the &quot;The Hunt&quot; section and somewhere like that in normal text and more properly called it something like &quot;Storyteller Advice&quot; or something, I would've liked it more. &quot;Content Warning&quot; is more about when you're about to watch a movie. What we're actually talking about here is that there's an example-chronicle in this book and there's advice for adjusting it based on what the people at your table want.<br /> <br /> If anything, there should be more of it. Storyteller-advice shouldn't just be about &quot;What if someone at your table doesn't like something from this pre-written Chronicle?&quot; and also address all sorts of adjustable stuff like &quot;What if I want this Chronicle about a mystery to have more action?&quot;. It's about enabling STs to make pre-written Chronicles their own and adjust them to the people they're playing with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511616#post1511616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the amount of cultures in the world, the variance, this is ALOT to consider. Hiring one or 2 cultural folk from one or two indigenous cultures does not cover the entire span of the world. You lot are asking for alot. Wasn\u2019t there 200 tribes alone in the pacific north west? There\u2019s 250 or so different version of Christianity. This is a large spread. They cannot possibly afford to hire enough consultants to cover all of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody's asking them to know and write about <i>all </i>the cultures in the world, but the ones they <i>do </i>write about or depict they should approach with respect and understanding (based on experts, research and maybe hiring writers with a suitable background). You don't just do it because it's nice but also in order to avoid mistakes. I doubt having to fix something this late before a release like the image in the GW-preview was a fun experience for the people involved. The more negligent the approach, the likelier it is, though, that it just leads to the creation of future issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T13:19:22-07:00","id":1511643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511628#post1511628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I now have read it and it feels more like a case of bad aesthetic choices. Both layout-wise by putting those things at the beginning of each chapter (and needlessly repeating it with the NPC-write-ups) and giving it a little &quot;box&quot; so-to speak is weird and calling it &quot;Content Warnings&quot; is also weird. After all, what it actually is trying to do is give Storyteller-advice with the notion of &quot;If you want to tone down the darkness of this story, here are the dials where you can turn things down a notch.&quot; Like, here's an example from Chapter 1 for people who don't have the book:<br /> <br /> Like I said, if you had it just put it at the beginning of the chapter after the &quot;The Hunt&quot; section and somewhere like that in normal text and more properly called it something like &quot;Storyteller Advice&quot; or something, I would've liked it more. &quot;Content Warning&quot; is more about when you're about to watch a movie. What we're actually talking about here is that there's an example-chronicle in this book and there's advice for adjusting it based on what the people at your table want.<br /> <br /> If anything, there should be more of it. Storyteller-advice shouldn't just be about &quot;What if someone at your table doesn't like something from this pre-written Chronicle?&quot; and also address all sorts of adjustable stuff like &quot;What if I want this Chronicle about a mystery to have more action?&quot;. It's about enabling STs to make pre-written Chronicles their own and adjust them to the people they're playing with.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nobody's asking them to know and write about <i>all </i>the cultures in the world, but the ones they <i>do </i>write about or depict they should approach with respect and understanding (based on experts, research and maybe hiring writers with a suitable background). You don't just do it because it's nice but also in order to avoid mistakes. I doubt having to fix something this late before a release like the image in the GW-preview was a fun experience for the people involved. The more negligent the approach, the likelier it is, though, that it just leads to the creation of future issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t disagree with you. And I haven\u2019t seen people here being unhinged, I\u2019m more referencing other areas or media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T13:21:30-07:00","id":1511644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511621#post1511621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trigger warnings are there to make sure no one is legit hurt. It is the same thing as the <i>Warning: Contains nuts</i> warnings on packages.<br /> <br /> And before anyone mentions the genre; If someone is allergic to shrimp, that allergy remains regardless of the type of food made. It is the same with trigger warnings, someone might LOVE Black Dog stuff, but they cannot deal with kidnapping scenarios at all.<br /> <br /> As for assuming malice, if you are making a high-profile product you have also to accept responsibility if things go wrong. This time it was a lazy artist, but that then means you might need to rethink hiring them again.</div> </div> </div> </div>this issue I have isn\u2019t the trigger warnings. It\u2019s the amount and frequency of them. See knightingale\u2019s above post. It\u2019s saturating. Vaesen by contrast has content warning: violence against children as a header to a story and that\u2019s it. (As an example). Content warning have been a part of the world of darkness. But since you seem to have misunderstood me for some reason, it\u2019s not the content warnings (obnoxiously done as they were), rather it\u2019s proof of intent. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T14:24:57-07:00","id":1511653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511609#post1511609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I got no publishing experience, so grain of salt, but how hard is it to ask a person whose job it is to know these things if something is offensive? In this case it was the artist derping about, but in general it shouldn't be hard to get input.<br /> <br /> Unless they don't want to change stuff at all and are just hoping to avoid the big controversies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not hard. They didn't do it.<br /> <br /> They don't want to change any more than they need to change to avoid controversies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511213-kikirpg-statement-issues-about-the-w5-preview-issue?p=1511616#post1511616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">people are quick to jump their ass about malice, intentional racism and all of this with zero idea of who these people are behind the screen. Demonizing with zero evidence of that. This isn\u2019t to say art theft is ok, stealing someone\u2019s image certainly isn\u2019t. But if the man\u2019s pic was part of a public domain reference this can happen.<br /> <br /> stop attributing malice when it\u2019s more likely ignorance. They are TRYING. They fixed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you missed James Sambrano's public statement about all this as a Native American RPG freelancer and diversity consultant that worked on the first iteration of W5?<br /> <br /> We can attribute malice here, because there's direct testimonial evidence of malice.<br /> <br /> Even if you want to claim some people jumped the gun here, and don't think it's proper to go the pattern of behavior negates ignorance route, everyone that saw malice in Paradox's corporate culture has some significant vindication that their judgement of what was going on was accurate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}